        <body>
            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="0377" n="307" xml:id="pg307"/>

                <head>No. 163.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sargent to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-11-13"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 13, 1882</date>.
                        (Received December 4.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 77.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor, referring to my dispatch
                    of November 6, being No. 74, referring to the exclusion of American hogs, pork,
                    and lard from Germany, to now inclose two very exhaustive articles from the
                    Berlin Tribune of the 10th and 11th instant, with careful translations. The
                    articles present very fairly the effects which the proposed exclusion would have
                    upon the trade of Germany, and upon the subsistence of the poorer classes, and
                    prove by irrefutable facts that the clamor against these productions is born of
                    prejudice. * * * The articles are written in admirable temper, and it is to be
                    hoped will have weight in showing to the German statesmen and public the truth
                    in a matter so important to the interests of both countries.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>A. A. SARGENT.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d163-a1.xml" xpointer="d163-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
